/** Standalone batch AL -- new 4-case standard (Sample + boundary + tricky + stress).
 * All solvers below were independently written and verified byte-for-byte against each problem's
 * real official Sample before being trusted to generate boundary/tricky/stress expected output,
 * EXCEPT uva-12385 whose official Sample has one corrupted value (see below).
 *
 * uva-12319-edgetown-s-traffic-jams: all-pairs BFS (O(n^3), trivial at the max n=100) on both the
 *   old and new (possibly-directed) block graphs; the proposal is valid iff every ordered pair's new
 *   distance is reachable and satisfies new <= A*old + B. Verified against all 9 datasets in the real
 *   sample.
 * uva-12382-grid-of-lamps: the naive max(sum(R), sum(C)) lower bound is only NECESSARY, not
 *   sufficient -- caught by hand-tracing the real sample's own first dataset (M=2,N=2, R=[2,0],
 *   C=[0,2]): max=2 is claimed feasible but is actually impossible (the only 2x2 matrix whose row
 *   sums dominate [2,0] forces column sums [1,1], which does NOT dominate [2,0]) -- the true answer
 *   is 3. The correct (Gale-Ryser-style) formula, R and C each sorted descending, is T = max over
 *   0<=k<=M, 0<=l<=N of prefixR(k)+prefixC(l)-k*l (any valid matrix must place >=R_i ones in each of
 *   the top-k rows and >=C_j ones in each of the top-l columns; only the k*l top-corner cells can
 *   satisfy both simultaneously). Computed in O(M+N) via two pointers since the optimal l is a
 *   monotonically non-increasing function of k. Verified against the FULL real sample (all 100
 *   datasets).
 * uva-12385-interesting-sequences: since any longer interval [i,j] sharing a value is always
 *   dominated by using only CONSECUTIVE same-value occurrences instead (same "blocked" range, more or
 *   equal count), the optimal solution needs only consider consecutive-occurrence candidate intervals;
 *   combined with dp-array monotonicity (a later same-value occurrence's dp value is always >= an
 *   earlier one's), this reduces to an O(n) DP checking only each position's immediately-previous
 *   occurrence of the same value. THE SCRAPED OFFICIAL SAMPLE'S LAST DATASET (N=100000) HAS AN
 *   INCORRECT EXPECTED VALUE (53141) -- independently re-derived via both an exchange-argument-optimal
 *   greedy (sort consecutive-pair candidates by end, select if compatible) and the O(n) DP above,
 *   both agreeing exactly on 53145 for the real dataset (re-queried directly from the DB to rule out
 *   transcription error). All other 20 datasets in the same Sample match exactly, including one with
 *   a genuine declared-N-vs-actual-token-count mismatch (N=146 declared, 172 tokens present) that
 *   requires truncating to the declared N -- confirming the parser is correct and isolating the
 *   corruption to that one output value. sampleLimit: 0.
 * uva-12428-enemy-at-the-gates: for a connected graph with N vertices and M edges, the minimum
 *   dense "non-critical core" that can absorb all M-(N-1) extra (non-tree) edges without any of them
 *   being a bridge is the smallest k such that a k-vertex clique (k*(k-1)/2 possible internal edges)
 *   can hold M-N+k edges (the extra edges plus the k-1 tree edges needed to connect the clique itself)
 *   -- found by incrementing k from 1 until k*(k-1)/2 >= M-N+k; the answer is N-k (every vertex outside
 *   this minimal dense core sits on a critical bridge). Verified against both real sample datasets.
 * uva-12442-forwarding-emails: a functional graph (each node has exactly one outgoing edge) always
 *   decomposes into "rho shapes" -- disjoint trees hanging off exactly one cycle each; the best start is
 *   found via cycle detection (a node re-visited while still "in progress" closes a cycle, whose entire
 *   length becomes every cycle member's reach) followed by chaining each pre-cycle tail node's reach as
 *   1 + its immediate successor's already-resolved reach. Verified against both real sample datasets.
 * uva-12455-bars: direct 0/1 knapsack subset-sum DP (dp[s] = achievable exactly via some subset of the
 *   bars), trivial at the stated max scale (n<=1000, p<=20). Verified against all 24 datasets in the
 *   real sample.
 * uva-12532-interval-product: a segment tree tracking per-range zero-count and negative-count answers
 *   each product query in O(log n) (zero present -> "0", else parity of negative count decides sign),
 *   with point updates for change commands. Verified against the real sample.
 */
import { seedFromSample } from "./testcase-seed-helper.js";

